# SLAAPS wind-tunnel profile B: control schedule ON (SLA_SCH_EN 1), 2x2 table, indicated airspeed 16 and 40 m/s x EDF command 0 and 1.
# Written 2026-11-21 (low knot lowered from 18 to 16 m/s so a 20.8 m/s true step, 18.4 indicated, keeps margin); replaces earlier versions. NOTHING HERE IS MEASURED. Load AFTER slaaps_vehicle.params and the trims file;
# it restates the revision-3 (40 m/s) base the table is built on, so it is correct even if profile A was loaded before it.
# Table method: moment derivatives = revision-3 values x (V/40)^2 (16 m/s knot x0.16). EDF knots hold the same values (EDF wash unmeasured).
# Rate gains are the revision-3 values at every corner: the allocator already divides by the scheduled authority, so do not also scale by 1/q.
# Entry gate: Manual enters only with indicated airspeed 16..40 m/s (positive, fresh), EDF command 0, density 0.9-1.35 (site density in the 2026-11-19 logs is 0.975, baro 83.4 kPa), battery 30-42 V.
# Below 16 m/s or above 40 the schedule rejects; mid-run it sends the supervisor to recovery. At rest Manual will NOT enter.
# Deflection per unit moment rises as V falls (x6.25 at 16 m/s): pitch/yaw full stick needs about 19 deg at 16 m/s against the 12 deg limit, so they clip at the low end.
# Linear interpolation overstates authority by up to about 22% near 22-25 m/s (loop gain about 18% low). Needs the pitot reading true speed with the right sign.
# Chosen limits, not measurements: density, voltage (= SLA_PWR_VMIN/VMAX), source age 0.5 s, filter 0.3 s, slews, transient rates.
# Data revision 5: declared Calibrated by the project lead, Kael Spry, on 2026-11-21 (SLA_DATA_STATE 1). Calibrated is not Qualified
# and not flight acceptance; see docs/SLAAPS_DATA_RECORD.md, revision 5.
